-- title:
--   Automorphism of the two-chart model induced by σ
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $F$ a field that is an $R$-algebra, and let $j \in F$ with $j \neq 0$. For a subset $S \subseteq F$, `chartAlg R F S` is the $R$-subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $S$; write $A_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the case $S = \{j\}$ and $A_{\mathrm{inf}} =$ `chartAlgInf R F j` for $S = \{j^{-1}\}$, and let $\mathfrak{X}(j) =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel R F j` be the pushout of the two morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the middle ring $\to \operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $\operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{inf}}$, with structure morphism `toBase R F j` to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ and chart morphism $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `ιFin R F j` from $\operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{fin}}$. Let $\sigma$ be an $R$-algebra automorphism of $F$ with $\sigma j \neq 0$. Assume: `toBase R F j` and `toBase R F (σ j)` are separated; `chartAlgInf R F j` and `chartAlgInf R F (σ j)` are of finite type over $R$; $\sigma j$ lies in `chartAlgFin R F j` and $j$ lies in `chartAlgFin R F (σ j)`; and, in both directions, every $y$ in one of the two pole chart algebras admits $s = 1 + j^{-1} a$ (respectively $s = 1 + (\sigma j)^{-1} a$) with $a$, $s$ in the other pole chart algebra and $s y$ there as well. Then there exist an isomorphism $w$ of $\mathfrak{X}(j)$ with itself and an $R$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ such that $w$ followed by `toBase R F j` equals `toBase R F j`; $\theta$ agrees with $\sigma$ on elements of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ viewed in $F$; $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ followed by $w$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\theta)$ followed by $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$; and the preimage under $w$ of the open range of $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ is that same open.
--
--   This is the functoriality of the two-chart integral model (the normalisation of the two-chart $j$-line) in the pair $(F,j)$: an $R$-automorphism of the function field whose effect on $j$ leaves the pair of charts comparable is realised by an automorphism of the model over the base which preserves the finite chart and is given there by the induced automorphism of the finite chart algebra. It combines the transport of structure $\mathfrak{X}(F,j) \cong \mathfrak{X}(F,\sigma j)$ with the comparison of two models of the same function field having comparable charts, and is used in the construction of diamond and Atkin–Lehner operators on integral models of modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_exists_iso_toBase_eq_and_iotaFin_comp_eq_of_algEquiv.lean

